{"name":"Saltwater Taffy","hex":"#d1ab99","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"saltwater taffy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A kind of soft taffy characteristic of the eastern United States, made with butter, glycerin, corn syrup, salt and water but not seawater."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/saltwater_taffy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Taffy (candy)","blocks":[{"text":"Taffy is a type of candy invented in the United States, made by stretching or pulling a sticky mass of a soft candy base, made of boiled sugar, butter, vegetable oil, flavorings, and colorings, until it becomes aerated, resulting in a light, fluffy and chewy candy. When this process is complete, the taffy is rolled, cut into small pieces and wrapped in wax paper to keep it soft. It is usually pastel-colored and fruit-flavored, but other flavors are common as well, including molasses and the \"classic\" (unflavored) taffy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Salt_water_taffy.jpg/330px-Salt_water_taffy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taffy_(candy)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Salt_water_taffy.jpg/500px-Salt_water_taffy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Salt_water_taffy.jpg/1280px-Salt_water_taffy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Salt_water_taffy.jpg/500px-Salt_water_taffy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASalt_water_taffy.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/The_Taffy_Shop%2C_Estes_Park_%282024%29-104A4619.jpg/500px-The_Taffy_Shop%2C_Estes_Park_%282024%29-